// Title: Antivirus Filter Driver Disallowed On Dev Drive - Registry
// Sigma ID: 31e124fb-5dc4-42a0-83b3-44a69c77b271
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @kostastsale, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-11-05 | Modified: 2024-08-16
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects activity that indicates a user disabling the ability for Antivirus mini filter to
//   inspect a "Dev Drive".
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1720419490519752955
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_devdrv_disallow_antivirus_filter.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\FilterManager\\FltmgrDevDriveAllowAntivirusFilter" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
